.TH CHTTPSVR_REQ_STREAM_ERROR 3 "2026-10-01" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_req_stream_error \- report why the last chttpsvr_req_read call failed
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpsvr_req_stream_error(const chttpsvr_req *req);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Reports why the last chttpsvr_req_read call on req returned -1.  It
has a meaning only immediately after such a -1 return.  The result is
unspecified at any other time.

It tells apart only the real transfer errors of chttpsvr_req_read that
depend on the data.  See chttpsvr_req_read(3).  It reports
ccol_success when caller misuse caused the -1 instead, and you cannot
tell that apart from "no error".  Two cases of misuse cause it: buf
was NULL while buflen was above 0, or
chttpsvr_register_streaming_handler did not register the route of the
request.  Both are static programming errors.  They happen on every
call to the code at fault, and not only sometimes.  A caller that hits
one is expected to find it and fix it in ordinary testing, and not to
diagnose it at run time.

Return values:
  ccol_timed_out             stream_read_timeout_us expired while the
                              handler waited for the next batch.  Or
                              the total body read time of the request
                              went above max_body_read_duration_us,
                              when you set that field.  Or the average
                              rate of the body fell below
                              min_transfer_rate_bps after the grace
                              period.
  ccol_msg_too_large         The body went above max_body_size in
                              mid-stream.  Or the declared size of one
                              chunk of a chunked Transfer-Encoding was
                              above max_body_size, before the server
                              read any data of that chunk.
  ccol_not_enough_memory     An internal allocation failed while the
                              server grew the body buffer.  The client
                              did not cause this.
  ccol_http_transfer_aborted The connection closed, or something reset
                              it, or the framing of the body was
                              malformed.
  ccol_success               There is no error on record for req, or
                              one of the misuse cases above caused
                              the -1.
  ccol_unexpected_failure    req is NULL, or its handle is invalid.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_req_read (3),
.BR chttpsvr_register_streaming_handler (3)
